Package: ac3spdif
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: pipewire, wireplumber
Suggests: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Description: Dolby Digital Live and DTS Connect for Linux
 Captures all system audio, encodes it to AC-3 (Dolby Digital) or DTS in real
 time, and bitstreams the result out an S/PDIF or HDMI interface as an IEC
 61937 data burst, so a receiver decodes 5.1 itself instead of being handed
 stereo PCM. What sound cards on other platforms call Dolby Digital Live or
 DTS Connect.
 .
 A virtual PipeWire sink becomes the system output; whatever plays into it is
 encoded in-process with ffmpeg's libraries and sent as a native passthrough
 stream to the digital output, or straight to the ALSA device for the lowest
 latency. Includes the ac3spdif-app tray application, the ac3spdif command
 line, which can run as a systemd user service from login, and ac3spdif-probe.
